# Python pipeline runs primarily in GitHub Actions; Vercel runtime
# is Node-first. ONE exception (post 2026-06-01): the Pulpo Pro
# Welcome instant-dispatch path runs a Vercel Python serverless
# function at api/internal/welcome-send.py. The function + its
# co-located requirements.txt MUST ship; its imported modules
# (automation/newsletter/**, pulpo/countries/**, web/data/ranked.json)
# are pulled in by the function's `includeFiles` config in vercel.json
# rather than re-included here, so the broad excludes below stay
# in force for everything else.
pulpo/
automation/
fixtures/
samples/
tests/
requirements.txt
*.py
__pycache__/
*.pyc
# Re-include the Vercel Python function tree. The function file +
# its co-located requirements.txt are matched by these negations,
# overriding the `*.py` and `requirements.txt` excludes above. The
# function's transitive Python imports (automation/, pulpo/) are
# NOT re-included here — they're pulled into the function bundle
# selectively via `includeFiles` in vercel.json so we don't ship
# the entire automation/ + pulpo/ trees to every Node function.
!api/**/*.py
!api/**/requirements.txt

# Local artifacts
.env
.env.local
DEPLOY.md

# Vite source (JSX) — built bundle ships from web/dist/, source isn't needed at runtime
new_ux/
docs/
nlp_keywords/
prompts/

# Node toolchain — Vercel installs from package.json itself
node_modules/